  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThis comes from this Chromium bug: https://crbug.com/505045915\n\nThe HTML spec [says](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics-other.html#selector-focus) about `:focus`:\n\n> an element has the focus when:\n> ...\n> its [shadow root](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-shadow-root) shadowRoot is not null and shadowRoot is the [root](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-root) of at least one element that [has the focus](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics-other.html#element-has-the-focus).\n\nThe question is: does that apply to elements that have **user agent** shadow roots? E.g. `<input>`, `<audio>`, `<video>`, etc.?\n\nHere's a test page, taken from the Chromium bug:\n\n- https://jsbin.com/cagoqad/edit?html,output\n\nThere are some interesting differences between browsers. It seems to me that the correct behavior would be to honor UA shadow roots for `:focus`.",
